-- title:
--   Uniqueness of Gauss-type valuations at level prime to q
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $5 \le q$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a nonunit of $A$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$, write $A_0 = A \cap k_0$ for the preimage of $A$ under $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and let $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lie in $A$; assume $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, has algebraically closed residue field, and that every $a \in A$ differs from some element of $k_0 \cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $\ell'$ be a prime with $\ell' \ne q$, $3 \le \ell'$ and $\ell' \nmid M'$, let $\xi \in k_0$ be a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity, and assume some ring homomorphism $k_0 \to \mathbb{C}$ carries $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$. Let $K''$ be the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(k_0)$ over $k_0$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField` of level $\ell'^2 M'$ with respect to the subgroup `levelH ℓ' M'` of $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell'^2M')^\times$, namely the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell')^\times$ (the units congruent to $1$ modulo $\ell'$), and assume $K''$ is an $A_0$-algebra compatibly with $A_0 \to k_0 \to K''$. Let $j'' \in K''$ be the nonzero element whose underlying Laurent series is the image under `coeffEmb` of the rational $q$-expansion `jq` of the modular $j$-invariant. Then any two valuation subrings $V, V'$ of $K''$ satisfying the three conditions: the image of $A_0$ is contained in the ring, the image of $\pi_0$ is a nonunit of it, and for every polynomial $P$ over $A_0$ not divisible by the constant $\pi_0$ both $P(j'')$ and $P(j'')^{-1}$ lie in it, are equal.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the classical statement that, over a henselian discrete valuation ring with algebraically closed residue field and at level prime to the residue characteristic, the Gauss (coefficientwise) valuation is the only valuation of the modular function field in which $j$ is a residually transcendental unit, in the tradition of Deuring's reduction theory and Igusa's Kroneckerian models. It feeds the identification of minimal primes over $\pi_0$ on the prime-to-$q$ level chart in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.le_of_mem_minimalPrimes_span_of_isPrime_chartAlgFin_of_coprime_level`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.le_of_mem_minimalPrimes_span_of_isPrime_chartAlgFin_of_coprime_level).
